{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261001_111734_3579b0", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_78aab10c0b084ef89511249f43fe0180 and its endpoint audit and bidirectionality design.\n\nThe findings support retaining both gene-regulatory and protein-environment explanations without ranking their contributions. Preventive LXR/NAC-associated protein recovery does not establish normal anatomy, delayed disease reversal, promoter rescue or NRF2 necessity.\n\nThe endocrine evidence adds a receptor-specificity limit: progesterone-responsive reporters and RU486 behavior do not establish a simple PR-dependent endogenous initiation mechanism. Conversely, PMP22-loss effects on ABCA1 localization and cholesterol efflux support a reverse PMP22-to-lipid direction, but not a closed transcriptional feedback loop.\n\nPreserved the FDFT1 context/matrix blocker. The existing selective source request remains unreplied; no duplicate is needed.\n\nLABBOOK q_8ff898e6200c4b4a is updated and synced. Artifact hashes were verified; no independent biological replication, new investigation or dispatch occurred.", "tokens": {"input": 24980, "output": 2470, "total": 739898, "cache_read": 712448, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 99795, "timestamp": 1791229307119}
